<title>USA: TABLE-Reebok Intl Q2 net income up 2.6 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Reebok Intl Q2 net income up 2.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOUGHTON, Mass. 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reebok International Ltd.</p>
<p>				     Three months ended June 30,</p>
<p>						1997	     1996</p>
<p> Net sales			$841,059,000    $817,572,000  (a)</p>
<p> Net income			 20,322,000	19,813,000</p>
<p> Net income per common share	  0.35		0.27</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>   outstanding		    58,576,000	73,922,000</p>
<p>					Six months ended June 30,</p>
<p>					     1997		1996</p>
<p> Net sales		     1,771,100,000   1,720,495,000  (a)</p>
<p> Net income			 60,506,000	68,228,000</p>
<p> Net income per common share	  1.03		0.92</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>   outstanding		    58,522,000	74,540,000</p>
<p>(a) Net sales includes revenues of the Company's Avia subsidiary which was sold in June 1996.  These revenues amounted to $22.6 million in the second quarter of 1996 and $49.4 million for the six months ended June 30, 1996, respectively.</p>
<p>	  ((New York Newsdesk 212-859-1700))</p>
